  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Smt Kiran Sengar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 30 July, 2025 Author: Anand Pathak Bench: Anand Pathak, Hirdesh Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Gwl:16069 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Anand Pathak & Hon'Ble Shri Justice Hirdesh On The 30th Of July, 2025 Writ Appeal No. 2205 of 2025 Smt Kiran Sengar Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh And Others Appearance: Shri Ajay Bhargava - Advocate for the appellant. Shri Ankur Mody - Additional Advocate General for the respon Order",
    "facts": "2. Grievance of the appellant is that vide order dated 23.08.2021, she was transferred from Guna and was posted at Morena. She actively participated in the campaign of preventing food adulteration in District Morena. Due to pressure of mafia involved in food adulteration, she has been transferred. Due to transfer of the petitioner, her entire family is suffering. Appellant submitted representation to respondent No.2 on 27.06.2025 but of no avail. Hence, she approached Writ Court by filing W.P.No.26347/2025. NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-GWL:16069 2 WA-2205-2025 3. Appellant has been transferred at the instance of food adulteration mafia as the petitioner was taking action against the said mafia. Appellant submitted representation against the transfer order, but of no avail. Learned Writ Court did not consider the aforesaid facts properly and passed the impugned order, which is liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 5 . Respondent/State supported the impugned order and prayed for dismissal of appeal.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the appellant submits that the Writ Court did not appreciate the facts of the case and passed the impugned order even without considering Clause 52 of the Transfer Policy.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the appellant submits that the Writ Court did not appreciate the facts of the case and passed the impugned order even without considering Clause 52 of the Transfer Policy.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
